ame>Hochstenbach</surname><given-names>PFR</given-names></name><name><surname>Franke</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Identification of novel autism candidate regions through analysis of reported cytogenetic abnormalities associated with autism</article-title><source><italic>Molecular Psychiatry</italic></source><year>2006</year><volume>11</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>18</fpage><lpage>28</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Castermans</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilquet</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Parthoens</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The neurobeachin gene is disrupted by a translocation in a patient with idiopathic autism</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Medical Genetics</italic></source><year>2003</year><volume>40</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>352</fpage><lpage>356</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12746398</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sultana</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Yu</surname><given-names>C-E</given-names></name><name><surname>Yu</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Identification of novel gene on chromosome 7q11.2 interrupted by a translocation breakpoint in a pair of autistic twins</article-title><source><italic>Genomics</italic></source><year>2002</year><volume>80</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>129</fpage><lpage>134</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12160723</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gillberg</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Wahlstr&#x000f6;m</surname>